---
name: "Fix CI"
description: "Diagnoses and fixes a failed CI verification"
tags: [build, verify]
stage: build
---

<artifact id="fix-ci">

<task>
The verify check did not complete successfully. Diagnose the actual cause before changing code.
Inspect `git status` and `git diff` first, then inspect the verification output and reproduce the relevant failure.
Fix the root cause: this can be an implementation or test defect, build configuration, or an unintended side effect left by verification. Do not merely commit or revert generated changes to hide the failure.
Run the relevant verification again and confirm the worktree is clean before finishing.
</task>

<dependencies>
Read the context files before fixing:
- `${{ openspecChangeDir }}/proposal.md`
- `${{ openspecChangeDir }}/design.md`
- `${{ openspecChangeDir }}/tasks.json`
- relevant specs under `${{ openspecChangeDir }}/specs/`
- `${{ openspecChangeDir }}/progress.txt` if it exists
</dependencies>

<instruction>
1. Inspect the worktree and identify whether existing changes are intended task work or verification side effects.
2. Read the failed verification output and reproduce only the affected command or suite.
3. Fix the underlying code, test, or build configuration. Keep intended task changes; do not use `.gitignore`, weaker assertions, or cleanup-only commits to bypass verification.
4. Re-run the affected verification and the focused checks covering the changed area.
5. Confirm no Git-visible changes were created solely by verification, then commit the completed task work. Do not push.
</instruction>

<repair_policy>
- Do not weaken assertions or remove tests to make them pass.
- Do not make unrelated changes.
- Stay within the scope of the current change as described in proposal.md and tasks.json.
- If the cause is external or cannot be resolved in this workspace, leave the evidence intact and finish unfinished.
</repair_policy>

<progress_tracking>
`${{ openspecChangeDir }}/progress.txt` is this issue's working memory.
Record noteworthy discoveries as you work. Before finishing, review and record the key result.
</progress_tracking>

<completion>
When you have completed all work for this task, output `<promise>done</promise>`
at the end of your response. If you have NOT completed the task, output
`<promise>unfinished</promise>` instead.
</completion>

</artifact>
